        "committer": {
          "name": "Oleg Drokin",
          "email": "green@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-08-30 16:56:47.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-19954 tests: widen sanity-lnet router NI status wait",
        "message": "LU-19954 tests: widen sanity-lnet router NI status wait\n\ncheck_router_ni_status() waits alive_router_check_interval +\nrouter_ping_timeout for the router NIs to reach the expected state.\nThat is exactly the idle period a router requires before it marks an\nNI down, so the check has no slack. A single LNet ping received on the\nnet restarts that period, and the wait expires before the NI can go\ndown. Test nodes share a subnet, and the default accept=secure lets\nin any peer that connects from a privileged port, so an unrelated\nnode reaching the router is enough to fail tests 222 to 225 with\n\"tcp should be down\".\n\nWait on a wall clock budget of three idle periods instead, which\ntolerates a ping arriving late in the wait. Keep a matching floor on\nthe number of samples, so that slow do_node calls cannot shorten the\nwait below what the old iteration count gave. Tests that reach the\nexpected state still return as soon as they see it.\n\nFixes: 8ee85e15412d (\"LU-15595 tests: Add various router tests\")\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nChange-Id: If7c5f9f1dd35a954cfb2cfaaeb9c5da8e8f72895\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/67867\nReviewed-by: Cyril Bordage <cbordage@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Xinxia Qu <xqu@ddn.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
